[quotes.thriving]
In full bloom. Practically showing off.
Grew a whole leaf while you were reading.
Photosynthesising pure literature over here.
Look at me. LOOK at me. I am flowering.
Absolutely thriving, you magnificent reader.
I am the best damn plant on this device.
Blooming. Actually blooming. Because of you.
Chlorophyll levels: obnoxious.

[quotes.content]
Two good leaves and no complaints.
Steady growth. Soil content. Life good.
Not the tallest. Not the saddest. Just right.
A chapter a day keeps the wilting away.
Green. Upright. Unbothered.
I have decided not to die today. Progress.
Perfectly average. I have made peace with it.
Photosynthesis going fine, thanks for asking.

[quotes.peckish]
Drooping slightly. Just saying.
The soil is getting a bit dry up here.
I lost a leaf. I am not blaming anyone.
Plants notice things. Plants remember.
One day. One bloody day and I am wilting.
Not to be dramatic, but I am dying a bit.
Would it kill you to read? It might kill me.
My stem hurts. Emotionally.

[quotes.neglected]
Wilted. The soil is dry and so is the mood.
I am ninety percent stick at this point.
Water is nice. Chapters nicer. I have neither.
Compost feels close. Prove me wrong.
You absolute weed. Look what you did to me.
Dying. Slowly. Pointedly. Where you can see.
I was going to flower. Now I am going to hell.
Neglected houseplant energy. Because I am one.

[quotes.milestone]
New record. I have grown an entire leaf.
Best streak yet. Look how tall I am.
Personal best. I am blooming out of spite.
Record broken. The soil is thrilled.
